+# Ascend gated RMSNorm
+
+The existing `tokenspeed_kernel.ops.layernorm.gated_rmsnorm` facade selects
+`ascend_gated_rmsnorm` on Ascend. The leaf is registered for vendor `ascend`
+only, with solution `ascend`, FP16/BF16/FP32 input signatures and
+`fp8_out=False`. Its portable-band priority is one above the generic Triton
+leaf, whose launcher uses CUDA. No runtime/model vendor branch is needed.
+
+This is an explicit **device-local eager PyTorch FP32 baseline**, not a fused
+or optimized NPU kernel. `launch_gated_rmsnorm` in the NPU package performs
+all tensor arithmetic on the inputs' device, with no CPU transfer, host reads
+of tensor values, JIT compilation or fallback. Direct CPU execution of this
+same helper exists for correctness tests; the registry leaf rejects CPU input,
+including when selected by a forced override.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `x` has shape `[..., width]` with positive width. A positive `group_size`
+  must divide width; `None` means the whole last dimension. All leading
+  dimensions, including empty ones, are preserved. Each row/group has its own
+  mean-square statistic.
+- `weight` is a vector of length width (per-feature weight) or group_size
+  (one vector broadcast to every group). `z` has exactly x's shape, or is
+  `None` for plain grouped RMSNorm. Strided rows, inner-strided inputs,
+  transposed leading axes and strided weights are supported.
+- `x`, `weight`, and `z` independently support FP16, BF16 or FP32 and must be
+  on the same device. Gate, reduction, reciprocal square root, affine and
+  gate products all compute in FP32. Only the final output rounds to x's
+  dtype. The fresh output has x's shape/device; no input is modified.
+- `sigmoid_gate=True` uses `sigmoid(z)`; otherwise the gate is
+  `z * sigmoid(z)` (SiLU). `norm_before_gate=True` computes
+  `weight * x / sqrt(mean(x²) + eps) * gate(z)`. Otherwise the statistic and
+  normalized numerator both use `x * gate(z)`. With `z=None`, the gate flags
+  have no numerical effect. The affine weight is outside the statistic in
+  both orders.
+- Every behavior argument is explicit. `weights_independent` is the existing
+  producer-scheduling hint, not a numerical option: both values preserve
+  eager stream ordering without PDL or early weight loads. `fp8_scale` must
+  be `None`; non-None raises `NotImplementedError` even on a forced leaf call.
+  Normal selection with `solution="ascend"` excludes FP8-output requests.
+  Invalid shapes/groups, unsupported tensor dtypes, and mismatched devices
+  raise `ValueError` rather than silently changing semantics.
+
+The family facade resolves `group_size=None` to width before dispatch. The
+helper also accepts `None` directly. Unsupported FP8 output is excluded from
+this leaf; the existing family's generic registrations are otherwise unchanged.
+No bitwise cross-vendor, fused-kernel, graph-capture, or performance guarantee
+is claimed. Floating-point reduction and sigmoid implementations can differ
+slightly from Triton while preserving its FP32 operation order and final cast.
+
+## Verification
+
+`test/test_gated_rmsnorm.py` uses an independent scalar Python float64 oracle
+with `math.fsum` and `math.exp`, not this implementation or the Triton/PyTorch
+family reference. The CPU/NPU matrix covers both gate orders/activations,
+whole-width/grouped/shared weights, no gate, FP16/BF16/FP32 and mixed dtypes,
+empty/vector/multidimensional shapes, strided views, large/tiny values,
+non-mutation and rejection behavior. Real NPU-only tests exercise the family
+facade, default registry preference, vendor/dtype/FP8 filtering, and forced-leaf
+rejections. There are no device mocks.
+
+From the repository root with the existing environment active:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH="$PWD/tokenspeed-kernel/python:$PWD/tokenspeed-kernel-npu/python:${PYTHONPATH:-}" \
+  python -m pytest -q tokenspeed-kernel-npu/test/test_gated_rmsnorm.py -k cpu
+```
+
+On the configured Ascend stack, source its CANN environment and run the same
+command without `-k cpu` to include direct NPU and public-dispatch tests. These
+checks do not replace Qwen3.5 end-to-end validation or establish graph capture
+and latency characteristics.
